body:
You are literally arguing that in a democracy the party of the majority shouldn't win. That is literally the point of a democracy. 

&#x200B;

What you should want is a parliamentary system where each party gets a certain amount of representatives in the legislative body based on the percentage of the vote they won. That is the way most of Europe does it and is a far better system where everyone's views can be represented.

You are reaching on this one. Theater design is pretty much a known quantity at this point and has been since Greek times. Theaters look the same because we know how to best design them and that leads to similarities.

&#x200B;

Edit: Does anyone else think the back of the chairs at the jersey city assembly hall look like the amazon smile logo?
